:.5in;
word-wrap:break-word'>

<div class=3DWordSection1>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>To build an autonomous <span class=3DSpellE>autocode</=
span>
agent with the mindset of a <b>System Architect</b>, you must move beyond
simple scripting and design a <b>Multi-Agent Orchestration</b> system. This
architecture separates concerns into specialized roles: high-level planning,
deep-dive technical research (scraping), and secure code execution.<o:p></o=
:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>1. Architect the Multi-Agent System<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>A robust <span class=3DSpellE>autocode</span> agent sh=
ould be
designed as a team of coordinated specialists. Use a framework like <a
href=3D"https://www.firecrawl.dev/blog/best-open-source-agent-frameworks"
target=3D"_blank"><span class=3DSpellE>LangGraph</span></a> for stateful,
graph-based control or <span class=3DSpellE>CrewAI</span> for role-based
execution.<o:p></o:p></p>

<ul style=3D'margin-top:0in' type=3Ddisc>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l11 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5i=
n'><b>The
     Architect (Supervisor):</b> Decomposes complex user requirements into a
     sequence of technical sub-tasks.<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l11 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5i=
n'><b>The
     Scraper (Researcher):</b> Specifically tasked with exploring <a
     href=3D"https://github.com/" target=3D"_blank">GitHub</a> for code pat=
terns, <span
     class=3DSpellE>StackOverflow</span> for bug fixes, and tool documentat=
ion
     for API schemas.<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l11 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5i=
n'><b>The
     Developer (Executor):</b> Writes and refines code in a sandboxed
     environment, iterating based on feedback from the Architect.<o:p></o:p=
></li>
</ul>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>2. Implement &quot;Seasoned Scraper&quot; Capabilities=
<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Standard LLMs have knowledge cutoffs; your agent needs
real-time access to the web.<o:p></o:p></p>

<ul style=3D'margin-top:0in' type=3Ddisc>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l2 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list .5in=
'><b>Targeted
     Scraping Tools:</b> Equip your Scraper agent with tools like <span
     class=3DSpellE>Firecrawl</span> or <span class=3DSpellE>Decodo</span> =
to
     bypass anti-bot <span class=3DGramE>protections</span> and render
     JavaScript-heavy documentation.<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l2 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list .5in=
'><b>Semantic
     Data Extraction:</b> Instead of raw HTML, use LLMs to extract only the
     relevant code blocks, API parameters, or error solutions from the scra=
ped
     content to save on token costs.<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l2 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list .5in=
'><b>GitHub
     Exploration:</b> Use the GitHub REST API to clone repositories, analyze
     file structures, and even submit pull requests for final review.<o:p><=
/o:p></li>
</ul>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>3. Design for Persistence and Memory<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>System architecture requires context that spans multip=
le
files and sessions.<o:p></o:p></p>

<ul style=3D'margin-top:0in' type=3Ddisc>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l6 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:list .5in=
'><b>Short-term
     (Conversation) Memory:</b> Tracks the immediate reasoning steps and to=
ol
     outputs.<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l6 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:list .5in=
'><b>Long-term
     (Knowledge) Memory:</b> Use a vector database like <a
     href=3D"https://getstream.io/blog/multiagent-ai-frameworks/" target=3D=
"_blank">PostgreSQL
     with <span class=3DSpellE>pgvector</span></a> to store and retrieve
     previously scraped documentation and architectural patterns across
     different projects.<o:p></o:p></li>
</ul>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>4. Ensure Execution Safety<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Never allow an autonomous agent to execute code on you=
r host
machine directly.<o:p></o:p></p>

<ul style=3D'margin-top:0in' type=3Ddisc>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l12 level1 lfo4;tab-stops:list .5i=
n'><b>Sandboxing:</b>
     Deploy code execution in isolated containers (e.g., Docker) or managed
     environments like <a href=3D"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DnNfi9H4=
mFFE"
     target=3D"_blank"><span class=3DSpellE>Genezio</span></a>.<o:p></o:p><=
/li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l12 level1 lfo4;tab-stops:list .5i=
n'><b>Human-in-the-Loop
     (HITL):</b> As an architect, include &quot;checkpoints&quot; where the
     agent must present its plan or final code for human approval before ta=
king
     high-risk actions.<o:p></o:p></li>
</ul>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>High-Level Architectural Flow<o:p></o:p></p>

<ol style=3D'margin-top:0in' start=3D1 type=3D1>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l1 level1 lfo5;tab-stops:list .5in=
'><b>Requirement
     Analysis:</b> The Architect receives a goal and drafts a &quot;System
     Design Document.&quot;<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l1 level1 lfo5;tab-stops:list .5in=
'><b>Research
     Phase:</b> The Scraper visits specific URLs (e.g., official docs, GitH=
ub
     repos) to gather technical implementation details.<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l1 level1 lfo5;tab-stops:list .5in=
'><b>Refinement:</b>
     The Scraper passes structured data back to the Architect, who adjusts =
the
     plan based on constraints found in the documentation.<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l1 level1 lfo5;tab-stops:list .5in=
'><b>Implementation:</b>
     The Developer writes code in a sandbox, running tests to verify the
     solution.<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l1 level1 lfo5;tab-stops:list .5in=
'><b>Deployment:</b>
     Once tests pass and the human approves, the agent pushes the code to
     GitHub.<o:p></o:p></li>
</ol>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Would you like to see a specific <b>Python scaffolding=
 code</b>
for the Scraper tool using one of these frameworks?<o:p></o:p></p>

<ul style=3D'margin-top:0in' type=3Ddisc>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l7 level1 lfo6;tab-stops:list .5in=
'><span
     class=3DSpellE>codenamev</span>/ai-software-architect - GitHub<o:p></o=
:p></li>
</ul>

