<p class=3DMsoNormal>Java Agent Development Framework<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Show all<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>build the fastest executing scaffolding - language bar=
rier
does not matter, but underneath everything should run as binary codes.<o:p>=
</o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>To achieve the fastest execution where every component=
 runs
as high-performance machine code, <b>Zig</b> is the optimal choice for your
scaffolding. It outperforms languages like Rust and C++ in raw cold-start
latency (8ms vs. 43ms) and binary size (287KB vs. 3.2MB), which is critical=
 for
an agent that frequently spawns and destroys sub-processes.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>1. The &quot;Binary-First&quot; Architecture<o:p></o:p=
></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>As a System Architect, you should build a <b>Self-Cont=
ained
Orchestrator</b>. This is a single, <span class=3DGramE>statically-linked</=
span>
binary that manages high-concurrency scraping and architectural reasoning
without the overhead of a virtual machine or garbage collector.<o:p></o:p><=
/p>

<ul style=3D'margin-top:0in' type=3Ddisc>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l13 level1 lfo7;tab-stops:list .5i=
n'><b>The
     Orchestrator (Zig):</b> Manages memory via <b>Arena Allocators</b>, wh=
ich
     are perfect for agentic tasks. You allocate all memory for a single
     &quot;research cycle&quot; and then free the entire block at once,
     eliminating individual <span class=3DGramE>free(</span>) call overhead=
.<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l13 level1 lfo7;tab-stops:list .5i=
n'><b>The
     Scraper Core (C/Zig):</b> Uses high-performance libraries like <a
     href=3D"https://ziglang.org/learn/build-system/" target=3D"_blank"><sp=
an
     class=3DSpellE>libcurl</span></a> or <a
